2026-11-18 23:16:10,896 - test - INFO - Existing record: {'id': UUID('01a1ef25-a72c-7b5d-ba6c-8435d25b1e73'), 'title': 'Ted Tackles Marriage and Fatherhood in Animated Series', 'link': 'https://businesstoday.com.my/2026/11/18/ted-tackles-marriage-and-fatherhood-in-animated-series', 'snippet': 'Reach Publishing Sdn Bhd 15-3, Block F1, Jalan PJU 1/42, Dataran Prima, 47301, Petaling Jaya, Selangor\nSeth MacFarlane’s foul-mouthed teddy bear is back, and this time, he and his best friend John have to contend with the indignities of middle age.', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 11, 18, 15, 53, 4, 51268, tzinfo=zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(key='Etc/UTC')), 'source': 'businesstoday.com.my', 'article_language': None, 'article_type': 'news', 'content': 'Seth MacFarlane’s foul-mouthed teddy bear is back, and this time, he and his best friend John have to contend with the indignities of middle age. Peacock has released the official red-band trailer for “Ted: The Animated Series,” a sequel to MacFarlane’s hit films that reunites Mark Wahlberg, Academy Award nominee Amanda Seyfried, and Jessica Barth with the franchise’s creator. Although Ted and John the prospect of marriage, children, and actual adult responsibilities doesn’t appear to have made them any more mature.\nUnlike Peacock’s successful live-action “Ted” prequel series, which followed John and his talking teddy bear during their teenage years in the 1990s, the new animated comedy moves the franchise forward. Set 12 years after the events of 2015’s “Ted 2,” the show finds John and Ted living next door to each other, both married, raising families, and stuck in dead-end jobs. Similarly to Peter from Family Guy, neither two have abandoned the recreational drug use, questionable judgment, or terrible ideas that made their friendship so enduring in the first place.\nWahlberg reprises his role as John Bennett, with Seyfried returning as his wife, Samantha, and Barth once again playing Ted’s wife, Tami-Lynn. MacFarlane, of course, voices the titular bear, while Kyle Mooney and Liz Richman join the ensemble as Ted and Tami-Lynn’s son Apollo (named after Apollo Creed from Ted’s favourite “Rocky” films) and John and Sam’s daughter Ruth, respectively.\nMacFarlane created the series alongside Paul Corrigan and Brad Walsh, who also executive produced the live-action prequel and serve as co-showrunners on the animated continuation. Rough Draft Studios handles the animation, with Fuzzy Door, UGT, and MRC producing.\n“Ted: The Animated Series” premieres with eight episodes on December 17 on Peacock, with additional episodes arriving in 2027.', 'content_status': 'completed', 'content_error': None, 'embedding': '[-0.014361823,0.01922219,-0.03253061,-0.022953559,0.024109691,0.01330429,0.0024587004,-0.00896892,-0.024283683,0.013845199,0.0023461117,0.010293716,-0.017709203,-0.035228707,-0.05071817,-0.04357092,0.010900078,-0.022868417,-0.035973627,-0.055914864,-0.010132255,-0.031619716,-0.0017146922,0.02840133,0.02912919,0.047889557,0.010838078,-0.04157092,-0.013183493,-0.02185038,0.021402184,-0.003371998,-0.01636457,-0.057351373,0.013339904,-0.05583687,-0.02293926,0.0031951205,-0.032139257,-0.009982057,-0.016141843,0.007038823,0.015930261,-0.03911701,0.020830233,-0.08879848,0.011609983,-0.00073028123,0.051056582,0.012391852,-0.026414922,-0.016011037,0.023369908,0.011170569,0.026723845,0.08211926,0.0067752725,0.054967746,-0.053299475,-0.024581289,-0.009865544,-0.012544616,0.0035881419,0.016045962,-0.03311913,0.08489812,-0.0071655354,-0.03496803,-0.02756156,-0.008179975,0.01722023,0.030004174,-0.03123198,-0.028936738,-0.042946637,0.059363954,0.012734635,-0.018830597,-0.013665101,0.038731787,0.03939651,0.005371286,-0.0301859,0.004286582,0.013950072,0.019582123,-0.0772429,0.06679802,-0.0017144686,0.010396159,-0.017238338,-0.022051325,0.0097412765,-0.03148667,-0.040758964,-0.021961074,-0.030535787,-0.0141932005,0.026955424,-0.01911961,-0.019768815,0.001364469,-0.03212261,-0.024250804,0.0038776526,0.03649375,